Sitting a long distance from the seals atop the pack ice and photographing them in the distance using my 600mm telephoto lense, I did anticipate the close encounter that was about to happen next!! 

From the crevases between the large ice pans this beautiful white coat emerges. In efforts not to startle or stress it I remained still. Once it realized I was of no value it moved on finally far enough away for this brief image. 

A very unwanted but unforgettable moment!!!

